WEBVTT

00:00.650 --> 00:02.840
Come on. Relax.

00:03.340 --> 00:08.570
As much as I'd like to interview 
you about yesterday's fire,

00:08.570 --> 00:10.610
we're off duty.

00:10.920 --> 00:12.490
It's our lunch break.

00:13.370 --> 00:16.410
So I thought I'd get my fortune told.

00:16.890 --> 00:18.200
How about you, Arase?

00:18.450 --> 00:20.710
I think I'll pass.

00:21.110 --> 00:26.170
What if he tells me I'm so 
unlucky I should quit the force?

00:26.600 --> 00:29.390
Nothing's ever easy with you.

00:30.490 --> 00:33.250
So, how about just me, then?

00:34.150 --> 00:35.440
Very well.

00:35.750 --> 00:37.710
Show him to the next room.

00:37.710 --> 00:38.970
Okay!

00:38.970 --> 00:41.730
Right this way! Follow me!

02:14.660 --> 02:17.980
Still, a student telling fortunes?

02:17.980 --> 02:22.200
That's not a problem if you register
 your business within a month...

02:22.520 --> 02:25.510
But forget all that red tape.

02:26.730 --> 02:28.830
Do me a favor, kid.

02:29.540 --> 02:33.380
Set this poor civil servant 
on the right path.

02:33.380 --> 02:37.090
I can't locate people 
who escaped from prison.

02:37.090 --> 02:37.920
Huh?

02:39.320 --> 02:43.460
Well, that's our job anyway.

02:43.830 --> 02:45.680
We'll figure something out.

02:45.680 --> 02:51.150
Besides, I'd rather try to prevent murders... 
If you can see the future and all.

02:51.550 --> 02:54.100
My readings aren't precognition.

02:54.540 --> 02:57.210
I merely trace paths.

02:58.260 --> 03:04.070
Both the path you have walked,
and the infinite paths spread out before you.

03:04.310 --> 03:06.410
He never looks that way at home.

03:06.410 --> 03:10.580
<i>Wow. He really looks the part.</i>

03:10.580 --> 03:13.830
<i>I guess he's seen his share 
of trouble, at least.</i>

03:14.640 --> 03:18.010
<i>If the fake Polka is doing something shady,</i>

03:18.010 --> 03:22.430
<i>I could snitch to these guys.
 They seem like cops.</i>

03:22.770 --> 03:26.470
I suppose I don't need to 
divine your profession.

03:26.470 --> 03:28.890
Well, it's not like I can hide it.

03:29.180 --> 03:31.270
Let me look closer.

03:31.270 --> 03:36.110
Around you, I see defenders 
of many people's safety.

03:36.630 --> 03:41.600
Countless hands that both 
chastise and shelter young boys.

03:41.600 --> 03:45.380
Against those who wield malicious blades,
they are shields.

03:44.700 --> 03:47.450
<i>So, he already knows I work
 for Community Safety.</i>

03:45.540 --> 03:49.310
At times, they become cords of 
steel to bind those weapons.

03:47.450 --> 03:52.020
<i>Takumi Kuruya is probably pulling 
this info from somewhere.</i>

03:50.090 --> 03:52.370
There is one who feels concern for you

03:52.370 --> 03:55.840
<i>I'd guess he's got an earpiece
hidden in that hood.</i>

03:52.780 --> 03:55.830
and wishes for your own safety.

03:55.830 --> 03:58.590
Iwanome from the Community Safety Division?

03:58.590 --> 03:59.840
Damn it.

03:59.840 --> 04:02.120
We just keep running into trouble.

04:03.240 --> 04:06.550
In your dealings with your 
ancestors and family,

04:06.550 --> 04:09.720
you will see many cards depicting 
members of the opposite sex.

04:10.810 --> 04:13.480
<i>He even knows about the matchmaking?</i>

04:14.130 --> 04:18.120
I see you still bear a 
grievous scar from your past.

04:19.440 --> 04:22.890
A wound as grave as a torn-off wing.

04:23.580 --> 04:29.490
So long as that wound weighs you down, 
your path will never escape the seabed.

04:29.890 --> 04:33.160
Well, isn't that fascinating?

04:33.160 --> 04:38.630
So, Mr. Fortune Teller,
will you tell me how to heal myself?

04:38.850 --> 04:42.090
Do you <i>wish</i> to be healed?

04:42.090 --> 04:43.690
I wonder.

04:44.080 --> 04:49.460
But if the person who gave me 
that wound has a path,

04:49.460 --> 04:51.600
I'd love for you to tell me about it.

04:51.890 --> 04:56.810
Your torn-off wing shall 
spell out a signpost for you.

04:56.810 --> 04:57.940
Huh?

04:59.620 --> 05:00.410
Whoa!

05:00.900 --> 05:03.940
Th-That one scared me a little.

05:00.900 --> 05:03.940
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

05:00.900 --> 05:03.940
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

05:04.450 --> 05:05.150
Hm?

05:09.290 --> 05:10.620
Wow.

05:10.620 --> 05:12.040
How does he do that?

05:12.040 --> 05:16.600
<i>I recognize this sound! It's the same 
as the writing I heard last night!</i>

05:17.210 --> 05:18.530
<i>I get it now.</i>

05:18.530 --> 05:22.760
<i>He was practicing this magic 
trick during that whole chat!</i>

05:30.640 --> 05:31.560
Iwa-san?!

05:35.070 --> 05:35.970
How...?

05:37.690 --> 05:39.020
Polka Shinoyama...

05:40.860 --> 05:42.300
What do you know?

05:43.670 --> 05:44.740
Iwanome.

05:44.740 --> 05:44.740
Hm?

05:44.990 --> 05:45.690
Whoa!

05:45.690 --> 05:48.660
You're treating me? Now there's a surprise.

05:48.660 --> 05:51.200
Hey, these are my favorite brand.

05:51.200 --> 05:54.200
Cigarettes don't suit me after all.

05:54.200 --> 05:55.060
Hm?

05:56.190 --> 05:57.790
What's this symbol?

05:57.790 --> 05:59.250
Memorized it yet?

05:59.250 --> 06:00.990
Well, yeah.

06:02.340 --> 06:03.460
Never forget it.

06:05.090 --> 06:05.850
Huh?!

06:06.270 --> 06:09.220
But never show this symbol to anyone else.

06:09.700 --> 06:14.390
It is both the signpost we must follow

06:14.390 --> 06:17.850
and a one-way ticket to death.

06:18.470 --> 06:19.980
Why did you draw this?!

06:20.920 --> 06:24.130
I merely showed you the path.

06:24.730 --> 06:28.670
Obey the dictates of your own heart.

06:33.940 --> 06:35.160
Sorry! My bad!

06:35.160 --> 06:37.290
I didn't mean to scare you!

06:38.120 --> 06:39.670
Here you go.

06:39.910 --> 06:41.540
This is your fee.

06:44.500 --> 06:46.800
Um... I can't accept this much money.

06:46.800 --> 06:50.890
Don't sweat it. I threw in extra 
because I wrinkled your outfit.

06:50.890 --> 06:53.760
Anyway, I think we're done here for today.

06:54.100 --> 06:57.980
Bye. Be seeing you, Polka Shinoyama-kun.

06:59.840 --> 07:01.280
The Corpse God.

07:02.640 --> 07:07.460
The one who told your fortune here 
is not Polka Shinoyama,

07:07.460 --> 07:09.280
but the Corpse God.

07:09.650 --> 07:14.330
If you say so. I guess a fortune 
teller needs a good name.

07:14.710 --> 07:15.500
But...

07:16.180 --> 07:17.830
I don't know about that one.

07:17.830 --> 07:20.970
It makes you sound like a troublemaker.

07:24.680 --> 07:26.470
What did he mean by "troublemaker"?

07:27.250 --> 07:30.050
Do you know those guys?

07:30.050 --> 07:31.890
They're policemen.

07:31.890 --> 07:35.430
Huh. It seemed like they 
came because of the fire.

07:35.710 --> 07:38.890
<i>The way that officer acted wasn't normal.</i>

07:39.300 --> 07:42.310
<i>What was written on that piece of paper?</i>

07:42.770 --> 07:45.770
<i>It might be tied to the fake Polka's secrets.</i>

07:46.360 --> 07:48.880
<i>Maybe I should do some digging.</i>

07:49.360 --> 07:50.570
Young miss.

07:51.150 --> 07:53.740
I'll run out to buy us dinner.

07:53.740 --> 07:55.750
Okay. Thanks.

07:55.750 --> 07:57.200
I'd like that.

07:57.530 --> 08:02.120
Buy shark stuff, too, if you get a chance.
I don't mind duplicates.

08:02.120 --> 08:03.430
V-Very well.

08:04.580 --> 08:08.550
<b><i>Curry
Restaurant</i></b>

08:04.580 --> 08:08.550
<b><i>Nancy</i></b>

08:04.910 --> 08:08.550
Nice, big chunks of meat. Tender shrimp.

08:09.120 --> 08:12.220
You savor the first bite,

08:12.220 --> 08:14.450
and then the spice hits you!

08:14.450 --> 08:15.930
I can't get enough!

08:15.930 --> 08:19.050
You always make that face here, Iwa-san.

08:19.050 --> 08:20.640
You look hideous.

08:29.110 --> 08:32.630
If you've got more to say to me, say it.

08:32.630 --> 08:33.680
This is so awkward.

08:33.680 --> 08:36.130
Oh? It's not a sore subject, then?

08:36.130 --> 08:38.470
I didn't really want to get into it,

08:38.810 --> 08:41.540
but eating away in silence is worse.

08:41.540 --> 08:42.870
I'll speak freely, then.

08:43.110 --> 08:44.860
What got into you back there?

08:44.860 --> 08:48.040
Oh, yeah. Sorry. I lost control.

08:48.040 --> 08:49.850
That isn't like you.

08:49.850 --> 08:52.630
Threatening people is <i>my</i> job.

08:52.870 --> 08:58.350
I'm the stick, and you're the 
poisoned carrot, remember?

08:58.350 --> 09:01.050
Hey, now you're quoting me.

09:01.410 --> 09:03.180
I can't argue with myself.

09:03.430 --> 09:06.650
What was written on that piece of paper?

09:09.170 --> 09:13.070
Sorry. Give me some time to get my 
thoughts in order while we walk.

09:13.070 --> 09:15.150
I'll tell you when we get to our next stop.

09:15.150 --> 09:17.610
All right. I'll wait.

09:17.610 --> 09:20.830
I'm relieved that you're 
back to your usual self.

09:21.070 --> 09:24.540
Yeah. I've got to keep cool, 
whether I like it or not.

09:25.030 --> 09:28.000
I screwed up because I got too heated.

09:29.340 --> 09:30.560
There they are.

09:31.860 --> 09:35.190
I think I'll shadow them 
a little while longer.

09:36.050 --> 09:39.770
<i>I bought food and shark 
merch at Village Vanguard,</i>

09:39.770 --> 09:41.640
<i>so I've done my job perfectly!</i>

09:44.890 --> 09:48.290
I laughed when I heard the 
Shinoyama house burned,

09:48.290 --> 09:50.610
but I never expected this 
place to go up, too.

09:51.400 --> 09:53.610
But, boss, isn't the safe fireproof?

09:54.620 --> 09:57.320
There's something I need to get out of it.

09:57.320 --> 09:59.530
Something you don't want the cops...

09:59.530 --> 10:02.470
<b>Fire Safety</b>

09:59.860 --> 10:02.510
...or firefighters to see?

10:02.510 --> 10:04.100
Cut the chitchat!

10:04.100 --> 10:05.280
Just keep watch for—

10:05.700 --> 10:12.340
<i>Click-clack, click-clack, it's begun.</i>

10:07.430 --> 10:08.420
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

10:08.420 --> 10:10.880
<b><b>Fire
Safety</b></b>

10:11.230 --> 10:12.340
Wha...?

10:12.930 --> 10:19.620
<i>The marching toys have come, rum-tee tum.</i>

10:14.050 --> 10:16.840
What the...?

10:19.930 --> 10:26.870
<i>Little toy soldiers, all in a row.</i>

10:26.870 --> 10:33.880
<i>Horsies and doggies follow, rum-tee tow.</i>

10:34.540 --> 10:35.440
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

10:35.440 --> 10:39.400
<b>Fire Safety</b>

10:36.150 --> 10:38.890
Damn summer bug.

10:39.400 --> 10:42.370
Suit yourself.

10:43.870 --> 10:46.240
I certainly shall.

10:47.650 --> 10:49.290
Round and round!

10:52.750 --> 10:55.190
Sheepskin parchment? No...

10:55.190 --> 10:57.050
And not pigskin either.

10:57.450 --> 11:00.760
Could this be... human skin?

11:01.500 --> 11:05.720
Is this the "bug" you mentioned, 
Fire-Breathing Bug-kun?

11:05.720 --> 11:08.680
I've picked the theme for 
my comeback performance.

11:08.900 --> 11:12.390
Let's all liven up the world together!

11:16.300 --> 11:18.740
Man, that sucked.

11:19.030 --> 11:23.690
But why'd that detective 
suddenly lose it like that?

11:23.690 --> 11:26.950
What did the ghosts haunting him tell you?

11:26.950 --> 11:29.580
No one was haunting him.

11:30.240 --> 11:32.040
What, really?

11:32.040 --> 11:35.640
Haunted people aren't all that common.

11:35.640 --> 11:36.670
In those cases,

11:37.180 --> 11:40.880
I use the information Takumi-kun 
digs up to offer advice.

11:41.230 --> 11:46.090
Wait, so you wrote something random 
down and it happened to set him off?

11:46.090 --> 11:47.470
No, the writing was—

11:47.780 --> 11:50.640
So, why did you hide it?

11:50.860 --> 11:55.060
Oh? What secrets do you 
think I'm keeping from you?

11:55.060 --> 11:58.270
To be honest, I'd given up hope.

11:58.270 --> 12:02.280
But, yeah... I guess I had to believe

12:02.590 --> 12:05.780
that you-know-who wouldn't 
give up the ghost that easily.

12:05.780 --> 12:07.240
What are you talking about?

12:07.500 --> 12:09.160
It's too late for games.

12:09.560 --> 12:12.700
Who could cover someone's 
tracks for five straight years?

12:12.700 --> 12:15.730
In this town, only you.

12:15.730 --> 12:19.800
I know that you have a connection 
to Polka Shinoyama, too.

12:20.050 --> 12:21.340
<i>Who is "you-know-who"?</i>

12:21.690 --> 12:25.640
Still, I sure didn't expect to get 
a message via fortune telling.

12:27.360 --> 12:32.140
What Polka Shinoyama wrote... 
no one but our mutual friend would know it.

12:32.610 --> 12:38.490
And aside from me, you're the only 
other one who might get told about it.

12:39.400 --> 12:43.370
I'm sorry. This isn't making sense to me.

12:43.750 --> 12:45.950
Which "mutual friend" is this?

12:47.400 --> 12:48.870
Don't play dumb.

12:49.100 --> 12:51.040
I was asked to stay out of it,

12:51.500 --> 12:53.410
and that's just what I did.

12:54.680 --> 12:58.230
So I don't know what was 
on that paper, either.

12:58.230 --> 13:00.370
It was too dark to see clearly.

13:00.370 --> 13:02.810
Huh? Hey, wait...

13:02.810 --> 13:04.970
You mean the one who wrote 
to that detective was...?

13:05.250 --> 13:10.470
The inspector the police shunned 
because we went wild together...

13:10.470 --> 13:13.060
And your precious senpai.

13:14.160 --> 13:15.350
Hosorogi-san.

13:15.650 --> 13:16.810
What? Then...

13:16.810 --> 13:20.280
Hosorogi-san knows that detective?

13:20.820 --> 13:22.840
Shinjuku is a surprisingly small world—

13:22.840 --> 13:24.820
But it has depth in equal measure.

13:23.910 --> 13:24.820
Ooh!

13:25.150 --> 13:28.110
Now there's a name that takes me back.

13:28.110 --> 13:31.580
Yeah. I haven't said it in a long time.

13:31.580 --> 13:36.030
You look happy... but a little 
angry at the same time.

13:36.030 --> 13:39.930
Can you blame me? I've been the 
only one stuck playing the clown.

13:40.440 --> 13:45.720
Well, if I'm pissed off at you,
it's more because of Polka Shinoyama.

13:45.950 --> 13:48.010
Has he done something to upset you?

13:48.010 --> 13:53.210
The point of the Community Safety 
Division isn't to shepherd children.

13:53.210 --> 13:58.120
It's to protect their past, present, 
and future. All three together.

13:58.450 --> 14:03.320
That was the policy, way back 
when Hosorogi-san was in charge.

14:04.500 --> 14:06.860
My, that's strange.

14:06.860 --> 14:11.280
Are you suggesting that Hosorogi-san 
recruited Polka—a child?

14:11.280 --> 14:15.690
Out of desperation, maybe? 
Or it was all your idea.

14:16.040 --> 14:20.330
If it's the former, I've got some complaints. 
All the more reason I want a reunion.

14:20.660 --> 14:25.050
We can't go dragging kids 
into our screwed-up problems.

14:25.280 --> 14:29.620
I certainly don't recall recruiting any.

14:29.620 --> 14:33.960
As for Polka Shinoyama-kun,
I simply rent a building to him as a favor.

14:34.330 --> 14:38.510
It's my chance to connect with a 
key figure in the Shinoyama Group.

14:38.510 --> 14:41.810
Do you think I'd let such 
a juicy fruit pass me by?

14:41.810 --> 14:47.420
I see. A self-interested favor 
<i>would</i> make a convincing motive.

14:47.730 --> 14:53.000
But you'd never have told him about 
Hosorogi-san if that were the real story.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.500
What if they got curious 
and did some digging?

14:55.500 --> 14:58.660
That kid would be in danger,
and so would the girl in glasses.

14:59.130 --> 15:03.290
After all, this was bad enough to 
force Hosorogi-san into hiding.

15:04.770 --> 15:08.080
You sound so certain that 
Hosorogi-san is still alive.

15:08.080 --> 15:11.800
I've received too much info that 
would make sense only to me.

15:13.310 --> 15:16.310
Fine, then. Play dumb if you want.

15:16.310 --> 15:18.520
But pass on the message.

15:18.820 --> 15:21.480
This time, I'll clean the rot out of the police,

15:21.480 --> 15:24.270
and make a place for 
Hosorogi-san to come back to.

15:27.090 --> 15:28.930
Clarissa, what was that about?

15:28.930 --> 15:30.400
Never you mind.

15:30.400 --> 15:33.590
But what if Polka-kun 
found Hosorogi-san's...?

15:33.590 --> 15:34.700
It doesn't matter.

15:35.080 --> 15:40.660
That old senpai of mine is far too
 obsessed with money to think of me.

15:40.890 --> 15:43.460
<i>Hosorogi and Clarissa.</i>

15:43.920 --> 15:47.380
<i>I'd better investigate this bar's staff.</i>

15:48.090 --> 15:53.100
<i>I'll crush every last pest that 
tries to get near His Lordship.</i>

15:54.090 --> 15:56.180
A police IA inspector?!

15:56.460 --> 15:58.080
What's that?

15:58.080 --> 16:01.190
A cop who investigates police 
corruption and stuff.

16:01.600 --> 16:06.190
Oh, I see. There were similar 
positions in my world, too.

16:03.000 --> 16:06.520
<b>Imperial Dazzling Corps

Office of Audit and Arrest

Deputy Commander

Jangrad Dimorigh XIV</b>

16:06.520 --> 16:10.680
So, you used to be those 
detectives' boss, Hosorogi-san?

16:10.240 --> 16:11.490
We were in different divisions.

16:11.760 --> 16:12.990
But we knew each other.

16:12.630 --> 16:14.030
For real?

16:14.030 --> 16:18.620
I can't believe this. Have you 
<i>ever</i> acted like an inspector?

16:18.620 --> 16:25.000
Heh heh heh... 
They called me "the delinquent inspector"
and "the filth that hunts dirt."

16:22.690 --> 16:23.740
That's so cool!

16:23.740 --> 16:25.000
Is it, though?

16:25.280 --> 16:29.460
So, what did you write on 
that paper, Hosorogi-san?

16:29.460 --> 16:32.340
If you're curious, 
pay me for the info.

16:32.490 --> 16:34.880
Are you <i>sure</i> you used to be an inspector?!

16:32.490 --> 16:37.430
My fee is one million! 
I won't take a yen less!

16:35.710 --> 16:37.430
But I need that money...

16:37.430 --> 16:39.660
Oh, there are endless ways to make money.
You're in good hands with me.

16:39.660 --> 16:41.070
What makes you so confident?

16:41.070 --> 16:45.260
Anyway, whatever you wrote is the 
reason that cop grabbed Polka.

16:44.750 --> 16:46.790
Indeed!
 For that, I humbly apologize.

16:47.380 --> 16:50.940
I hate to drag you into this,
but it involves one of my regrets.

16:51.210 --> 16:53.830
In that case, I guess I don't have a choice.

16:53.830 --> 16:55.280
What do you mean?

16:55.280 --> 17:00.220
In exchange for services,
 I'll resolve some of Hosorogi-san's regrets.

17:00.220 --> 17:02.870
That was our pact.

17:02.870 --> 17:07.230
Without regrets,
won't Hosorogi-san just move on?

17:07.230 --> 17:09.310
I'm not as ungrateful as all that!

17:09.310 --> 17:13.920
If those officials work well, 
will you have one less regret?

17:13.920 --> 17:17.930
Well, I can only hope it works.

17:15.270 --> 17:16.380
I suppose so.

17:16.970 --> 17:17.930
<i>Regrets, huh?</i>

17:18.470 --> 17:21.700
<i>One of these days,
I'll have to face up to Lisa.</i>

17:22.060 --> 17:24.020
Tokyo 
Detention
House

17:23.220 --> 17:25.820
The world is smaller than it seems.

17:25.820 --> 17:27.940
If you truly desire a reunion,

17:28.210 --> 17:30.570
it's surprisingly easy to achieve.

17:31.060 --> 17:32.650
Don't you agree,

17:32.970 --> 17:38.110
Prisoner No. 243291343432497-kun?

17:38.780 --> 17:41.910
You made up that number at random.

17:42.490 --> 17:45.370
That can't be what you came 
all the way here to say,

17:45.640 --> 17:49.330
Ten'a Sorimura... Or should I say
 the Phantom Solitaire?

17:50.250 --> 17:53.840
Then I suppose I'll call you Grocer-kun!

17:53.840 --> 17:59.970
Still, I'd hoped for a bit more surprise, 
or at least a laugh at my number gag.

18:00.250 --> 18:04.440
If you want me to laugh,
offer me something worth laughing at.

18:04.440 --> 18:08.560
If my enjoyment outweighs my laughter, 
I'll refund you the difference.

18:08.560 --> 18:12.350
Oh, well. I'll get a laugh 
out of you eventually.

18:12.350 --> 18:14.890
I'm just here to shop today.

18:14.890 --> 18:17.780
We appreciate your patronage.

18:17.780 --> 18:19.240
I'd like to buy

18:19.490 --> 18:20.910
information.

18:20.910 --> 18:24.700
Everything you know about 
this symbol, if you please.

18:24.700 --> 18:26.740
I recognize it, of course.

18:26.740 --> 18:27.910
Now then,

18:28.400 --> 18:30.760
let's talk price.

18:30.760 --> 18:34.000
I'll accept information worth 
beginning to tell you for.

18:35.920 --> 18:37.760
<i>The Grocer—</i>

18:38.250 --> 18:40.240
<i>According to metropolitan police records,</i>

18:40.240 --> 18:43.970
<i>the name originates in a merchant 
family with a century of history.</i>

18:43.970 --> 18:48.580
<i>And now this man, arrested by Tsubaki Iwanome,</i>

18:48.580 --> 18:54.610
<i>is supposedly the fifth-generation 
owner of this family business.</i>

18:54.610 --> 18:59.050
<i>He is also an anomaly in this 
strictly regulated prison.</i>

18:59.050 --> 19:06.200
<i>The fact that this space is permitted 
speaks to the Grocer's true nature.</i>

19:06.200 --> 19:08.580
<i>The state of this solitary cell</i>

19:08.580 --> 19:15.520
<i>testifies to the power that he 
gained by dealing with the state.</i>

19:15.520 --> 19:20.440
<i>It is neither the pen nor the sword, but trade
 which is the most blatant form of might.</i>

19:20.440 --> 19:25.220
<i>Everything is on the table, from human 
lives to the fates of nations,</i>

19:25.440 --> 19:30.310
<i>as well as goods—mass-produced,
 limited, stolen, lost, and sacred.</i>

19:30.310 --> 19:34.560
<i>The sole exception is their own minds.</i>

19:35.620 --> 19:38.780
Although I'm not fond of violence,

19:38.780 --> 19:43.240
when I must fight,
I fight with playing cards.

19:43.490 --> 19:44.490
And why...

19:45.260 --> 19:46.570
...do you think...

19:47.700 --> 19:51.730
...that all people have used 
cards as weapons since antiquity?

19:51.730 --> 19:55.820
Pardon our ignorance, but our 
store knows of no such history.

19:55.820 --> 19:57.300
The answer is simple:

19:57.300 --> 19:59.010
Because it's cool!

20:00.450 --> 20:01.440
I see.

20:01.930 --> 20:05.270
You've wasted my time. 
That will cost you dearly.

20:05.270 --> 20:06.470
What?!

20:06.470 --> 20:07.750
Not so fast!

20:07.750 --> 20:13.070
You asked for information to begin our talk, 
so I gave you my very best!

20:13.070 --> 20:16.020
Your idea of quality mystifies me.

20:16.020 --> 20:20.770
In this store, at least, the Phantom 
Solitaire's stock has plummeted.

20:19.780 --> 20:23.780
<b>Solitaire</b>

20:20.770 --> 20:22.070
Be reasonable!

20:22.070 --> 20:23.780
I wish <i>you</i> would.

20:23.780 --> 20:26.750
Fine, then! One more exclusive tidbit!

20:26.750 --> 20:27.710
Oh?

20:27.710 --> 20:33.330
Rubbing your hands with oil slightly 
reduces the risk of paper cuts.

20:28.760 --> 20:33.330
<b>GOOEY</b>

20:28.760 --> 20:33.330
<b>SLIMY</b>

20:30.770 --> 20:33.330
<b>STICKY</b>

20:33.330 --> 20:36.290
Why not just wear rubber 
gloves or use hand cream?

20:37.450 --> 20:41.890
Learning that a master criminal like 
you is actually a complete fool

20:41.890 --> 20:44.220
is worth something, I suppose.

20:44.220 --> 20:45.770
Mind your manners.

20:45.770 --> 20:49.430
Please allow us to offer 
you all we can in exchange.

20:49.740 --> 20:52.560
<b>Tasty Stick</b>

20:49.880 --> 20:51.260
This should do.

20:51.260 --> 20:52.560
Thirty yen?!

20:52.560 --> 20:53.520
All right!

20:53.520 --> 20:56.540
I'll take them because they're tasty, 
but you can't distract me with food!

20:56.540 --> 21:00.020
Give me the information I came here for!

21:00.520 --> 21:03.720
The symbols on playing 
cards all have meaning.

21:03.720 --> 21:04.530
Yes?

21:04.810 --> 21:09.610
On French cards, spades are swords,
clubs are clubs,

21:09.610 --> 21:13.120
hearts are chalices,
and diamonds are coins.

21:13.680 --> 21:18.920
Almost every symbol in this world,
no matter how simplified,

21:18.920 --> 21:22.230
is likewise imbued with some significance.

21:22.660 --> 21:23.590
For example,

21:23.990 --> 21:27.050
this diagonal line signifies a sword.

21:27.430 --> 21:32.690
An old knight order in central and 
eastern Europe used a similar insignia,

21:32.690 --> 21:34.850
but the two are completely unrelated.

21:35.160 --> 21:38.170
Now, that concludes your free sample.

21:38.170 --> 21:41.980
You must purchase more with 
information of equal value.

21:41.980 --> 21:43.170
Very well.

21:43.170 --> 21:46.260
This is for my performance. 
I'll pay whatever you ask.

21:46.260 --> 21:47.430
Are you certain?

21:48.260 --> 21:52.910
We adjust our prices to our 
customers' circumstances.

21:53.280 --> 21:55.170
And by "circumstances," we do not mean

21:55.170 --> 21:58.700
the contents of their wallets.

22:09.230 --> 22:13.430
<i>Well, today is the day that 
the Phantom Solitaire set.</i>

22:13.430 --> 22:15.530
<i>Have there been any developments?</i>

22:15.530 --> 22:17.000
Oh, that's today?

22:17.000 --> 22:19.500
I can't wait to find out what he'll do!

22:19.500 --> 22:22.550
Well, terrorist bombing 
doesn't seem like his style.

22:22.550 --> 22:23.930
Morning.

22:24.820 --> 22:26.500
Nice day, huh?

22:26.500 --> 22:27.780
It's already noon.

22:27.780 --> 22:32.960
Don't worry. Bedroom security officers 
don't need to make that distinction.

22:32.960 --> 22:34.790
What's reassuring about that?

22:34.790 --> 22:35.700
Good morning!

22:35.700 --> 22:36.810
Morning.

22:44.880 --> 22:46.750
Hey, what's that?

22:47.190 --> 22:47.760
Hm?

22:51.410 --> 22:53.480
Oh, wow!

22:55.140 --> 22:58.950
<i>Oh, it looks like something 
just happened in Shinjuku!</i>

22:58.950 --> 23:00.140
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

23:04.610 --> 23:07.370
<i>The sky is full of blimps.</i>

23:10.390 --> 23:11.530
How...?

23:15.250 --> 23:19.660
I thought I reincarnated 
to a different world.

23:20.060 --> 23:22.630
Do you recognize that symbol, Polka-kun?

23:23.640 --> 23:25.140
I'm sure of it.

23:26.150 --> 23:27.170
That's...

23:28.670 --> 23:33.480
...the emblem of the fallen 
empire from my old world.
